                                                "sense_id": "ef2f46e3-b38e-313b-b5a8-0cea37b5142a",
                                                "text": "The Nashville's cousin, the Tennessee warbler, is just as badly named: neither can be found in Tennessee, except during migration. Tennessees vary a lot in fall; some are almost pure white below, mimicking spring plumage, while immatures like the one pictured on page 304 can be quite yellow below."
